Lately, there has been a LOT of discussion over which weighs more,
dragon scale mail, mithril, plate mail, etc.  Frustrated over the
contention (and curious about the REAL answer), I decided to surf 
the source, and extracted the following table from objects.c.
This is for the distribution version of NH 3.1.3, and is _not_
dependant on platform.  Note also that the "special" armors
(like helm of brilliance, opposite alignment, etc.) are not 
guaranteed to match the "other name"s in this list - they are
randomly assigned at startup (checked this out briefly in 
wizard mode).  To figure out which is a better AC, subtract the
AC number from 10 - this is how far undamaged, unenchanted armor
of that type will take your AC down.

To the point of recent contention - 
Dragon scale mail (of any color) is the _lightest_ armor worth
having (I don't count a leather jacket as worth having :), by
a significant margin.  Mithril is great until you get dragon
scale, but I would take even yellow dragon scale mail (no SPFX)
over mithril any day.

Red dragon scale mail on, ready for flames :-)

Frank

